vhost-user-gpu: answer updates a display draws without blocking

The backend waits for an answer to each DMABUF_UPDATE, which QEMU sends when
the console reports the frame as flushed: when the display unblocks it. With
patch 0001, SPICE draws a local client's updates without blocking the console,
so that never happens and the backend (and the guest's GPU) would stop after
the first frame. Answer right away when the update left the console unblocked
and wasn't answered already.

--- a/hw/display/vhost-user-gpu.c
+++ b/hw/display/vhost-user-gpu.c
@@ -338,6 +338,16 @@
         }
         g->backend_blocked = true;
         qemu_console_gl_update(con, m->x, m->y, m->width, m->height);
+        /*
+         * A display that draws without blocking the console (SPICE, local
+         * client) never reports the frame as flushed: answer right away,
+         * unless it was answered meanwhile (a display that reports the flush
+         * from within the update)
+         */
+        if (g->backend_blocked && !qemu_console_is_gl_blocked(con)) {
+            vhost_user_gpu_unblock(g);
+            g->backend_blocked = false;
+        }
         break;
     }
 #ifdef CONFIG_PIXMAN
